WEBVTT

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:19.320
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.070
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.810
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.020
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:59.250
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:35.520
In exchange for plane fare, we entered the KC Grand Prix duel tournament.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:41.530
I don’t like being used as a promotional tool for Kaiba, but it’s nice to duel for fun.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.830
My opponent is the annoying Sieg Lloyd.

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:52.230
He looks down on others, but I'll put him in his place in this duel!

00:01:54.330 --> 00:02:00.330
Goddess of Monster Destruction

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.850
I activate my spell card!

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:10.710
Ride of the Valkyries!

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.530
This card Special Summons all Valkyries in my hand.

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:23.880
Descend, my fighting maidens!

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:39.470
He instantly summoned four monsters!

00:02:40.140 --> 00:02:43.120
It’s too late to regret this.

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.360
Watch!

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:47.410
I activate Valkyrie Zweite’s effect!

00:02:47.410 --> 00:02:52.890
When it's summoned, one of your monsters is destroyed.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.090
I activate Valkyrie Erste’s effect.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.580
By removing one of your monsters from play-

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:10.030
Of course I’m talking about your Jinzo.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:15.980
My monster uses those attack points to attack with this turn.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:17.100
What?

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.790
You have no time to mourn for your monster.

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.230
Valkyrie Erste, attack him directly!

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:26.150
Watch out, Jonouchi!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.260
Jonouchi!

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:34.060
The three Valkyrie Zweites also attack you directly!

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.060
Jonouchi!

00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:44.380
I told you that you’re no match for me.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.820
Too bad, but I haven’t lost yet!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.240
Jonouchi!

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:54.410
Impossible!  You should have no life points left!

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.820
During your first attack, I activated this!

00:03:58.820 --> 00:04:01.350
The spell card, Hyper Refresh!

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.120
I can activate it when I have no monsters...

00:04:04.120 --> 00:04:09.740
...and your monsters’ total attack points are greater than my life points.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:12.150
It doubles my life points!

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:16.480
How’s that!  I’m pretty tough!

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:19.480
Your resistance is pointless.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.910
I set one card.

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:24.080
I end my turn.

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:30.780
The Valkyries I Special Summoned using Ride of the Valkyries return to my deck at the end of the turn.

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.230
Take a break, my Valkyries.

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:42.900
You may act cool, but you have no monsters on your field to protect you!

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.760
I’ll end you next turn!

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:53.220
Cutting data influx.  Protocol shutdown.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:54.750
Erasing memory.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.780
Access standby.  Download complete.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:00.120
I won’t let you do whatever you want!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.420
It’s back to normal.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:09.020
Okay!  My turn!

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:12.740
- It stopped!
-The system’s restored!

00:05:12.740 --> 00:05:14.300
It's fixed!

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.070
It stopped.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.050
It’s finally quiet.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:22.720
Something is definitely wrong.

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.340
I’m going to my brother!

00:05:25.900 --> 00:05:30.880
This was a simple trick for Kaiba to fix.

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:33.780
But will he be able to find me?

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:42.930
You need great intellect and skill to break into Kaiba Corporation’s main computer.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.300
It bothers me.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:57.100
Isono, carefully check Sieg Lloyd’s background.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.890
Especially if there’s a connection with Germany's Schroeder family.

00:06:00.890 --> 00:06:02.780
The Schroeder family?

00:06:02.780 --> 00:06:10.120
I met him a long time ago at a lame party that Gozaburo held to form economic ties in Europe.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:16.120
He would've been able to do these things.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:21.200
Go for it, Jonouchi!

00:06:21.640 --> 00:06:23.930
My turn!  I draw!

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:29.170
I summon Swordsman of Landstar in attack position!

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:31.280
Here I go!

00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:34.020
Swordsman of Landstar attacks you directly!

00:06:34.540 --> 00:06:37.280
I activate my trap card.

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.480
Fricka's Mediation.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:44.580
By removing Wotan's Judgment in my graveyard from play...

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:47.350
...I negate battle damage this turn.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:51.460
I won't let you touch me anymore.

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.990
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.000
My turn.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.660
It seems fate loves me.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.640
I activate a spell card from my hand.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.740
Nibelung's Treasure.

00:07:10.740 --> 00:07:17.490
It lets me take Nibelung's Ring from my deck and place it on your field.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:21.140
I equip Nibelung's Ring on your monster.

00:07:22.280 --> 00:07:24.960
And I draw five cards.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:27.410
What's with this ring?

00:07:27.410 --> 00:07:31.080
I activate a spell card from my hand.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:34.720
The three goddess sisters who control destiny...

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:38.820
Spin the threads of the past, present and future.

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:41.340
The three Norn sisters, come forth!

00:07:41.340 --> 00:07:45.070
The Continuous Spells, Goddess Urd's Verdict!

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:47.780
Goddess Verdande's Guidance!

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:50.720
Goddess Skuld's Oracle!

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.150
Three goddesses?

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:56.150
Goddess Skuld controls the future.

00:07:56.150 --> 00:07:58.590
Show me what future comes!

00:08:01.530 --> 00:08:08.510
Once per turn, I can see the top three cards in your deck and rearrange them.

00:08:08.510 --> 00:08:10.280
What?

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:13.210
What’s he going to do by looking at his opponent’s deck?

00:08:18.480 --> 00:08:21.530
I'll change the order of those three cards.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.520
Put the second card on top.

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.950
What’s he planning to do?

00:08:28.950 --> 00:08:32.770
Next, Goddess Verdande controls the present.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:39.550
Once per turn, I guess the type of the top card in your deck.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.410
If I’m correct...

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:45.290
It must be set on your field.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:45.940
What?

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:50.370
The top card in your deck is a monster card!

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:53.380
You know because you saw it!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:56.600
The monster is summoned facedown in defense position.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:08:58.330
Fine!

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.020
Urd controls the past.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:05.580
Show me how this fool looks.

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:10.960
Once per turn, I guess your set card.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:15.020
If I’m correct, that card is removed from play.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:15.900
What?

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.150
No way!

00:09:17.150 --> 00:09:18.900
Of course he’ll get it right!

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.530
This isn't fair!

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:24.240
The set card is Panther Warrior.

00:09:25.280 --> 00:09:27.440
Go to Valhalla!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:32.390
My Panther Warrior...

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:35.680
First Jinzo, now Panther Warrior!

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.950
All his powerful monsters!

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.360
This is bad!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.360
I end my turn.

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:46.650
What’s wrong?  Learned how powerless you are against my gods?

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.230
Damn!  Such annoying moves!

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.760
My turn!  I draw!

00:09:52.760 --> 00:09:55.880
Nibelung's Ring now activates!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.040
What?

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:02.350
You no longer control the monster equipped with that card.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.310
But you can draw two cards during your Draw Phase.

00:10:06.310 --> 00:10:08.530
Doesn’t that benefit me?

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:10.440
What are you thinking?

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:12.360
You think it does?

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:18.610
There’s no point feeling confused!

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:19.260
I draw!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.940
You've been cursed by the gods.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:24.440
You can no longer escape!

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:25.100
What?

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:28.100
Due to Nibelung's Ring’s effect...

00:10:28.100 --> 00:10:33.540
...if you drew a monster card, you must discard one monster.

00:10:33.540 --> 00:10:35.140
Say what?

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.940
Goddess Skuld sees the future.

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:43.600
One of your cards is a monster card - Knight of Dark Dragon.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.460
Send it to the graveyard.

00:10:49.140 --> 00:10:53.060
If nothing changes, Jonouchi can't use his monster cards.

00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:58.790
His deck uses Goddess combos to remove cards from his opponent’s deck...

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:04.050
...make sure they can’t be revived, and use Nibelung's Ring to send more monsters to the graveyard.

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:06.210
It’s a card destruction deck.

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:28.870
Even if I draw a monster card, it’ll be removed before it comes to my hand.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:31.420
And he knows what cards are in my hand.

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:36.210
Unless I can draw a card without him knowing what it is, I can't win.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.140
I activate a spell card from my hand!

00:11:40.680 --> 00:11:44.090
The Continuous Spell, Dangerous Machine Type-6!

00:11:44.650 --> 00:11:48.250
During each of my Standby Phases, I pull the slot machine!

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:51.520
Depending on the number I get, a different effect activates!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:54.020
I’m luckier than most people!

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:56.170
They say luck is a part of skill!

00:11:56.660 --> 00:11:58.410
He shouldn’t admit that.

00:11:58.410 --> 00:12:02.080
You think you can win with luck only?

00:12:02.080 --> 00:12:04.850
When fate loves me?

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:08.320
You're gonna find out next turn!

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.500
I end my turn!

00:12:09.500 --> 00:12:12.090
My turn.  I draw.

00:12:12.520 --> 00:12:15.300
I activate the three sister goddesses' effects.

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:20.050
Place the second card on top.

00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:27.160
The top card is the monster card, Goblin Attack Force.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.960
Another monster is gone.

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:36.900
Jonouchi...

00:12:36.900 --> 00:12:41.090
I set a card and end my turn.

00:12:41.090 --> 00:12:44.080
My turn!  I draw!

00:12:44.080 --> 00:12:46.420
You must've drawn a monster card.

00:12:46.420 --> 00:12:48.320
Discard it.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:55.490
But my Continuous Spell, Dangerous Machine Type-6 activates!

00:12:58.450 --> 00:12:59.460
All right!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:03.160
3 lets me draw a card.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:06.740
And the other card I drew was also a monster card!

00:13:08.160 --> 00:13:12.100
I summon Sasuke Samurai in attack position!

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.060
No matter what you do, it’s pointless.

00:13:18.700 --> 00:13:22.260
I activate my Continuous Trap, Loge's Flame.

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:24.780
What?

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:31.730
As long as it's on the field, monsters with 2000 or lower attack points can't attack.

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:34.730
But I'll also activate my set card!

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.050
Graceful Dice!

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:42.900
A monster with 500 or lower attack points has it multiplied by the number I roll!

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:48.000
Let's see who’s luckier - me or you!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:50.300
If he rolls a 5 or 6, he wins!

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:51.140
Please work!

00:13:56.980 --> 00:14:00.750
Fate loves me instead of you.

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:06.830
No way...

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:09.860
I couldn't do a thing.

00:14:12.340 --> 00:14:16.000
Darling, are you watching?  I won!

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:24.200
Damn!  I can’t believe I lost at luck!

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:28.100
But on the bright side, he didn't see what this trap card was.

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:32.080
I set a card and end my turn!

00:14:32.890 --> 00:14:34.750
My turn.  I draw.

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:36.790
I activate my goddess combo.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:41.120
Place the second card on top.

00:14:45.560 --> 00:14:49.930
Another monster’s soul is sent to Valhalla.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:53.000
I activate my spell card!

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.930
Swan Maiden!

00:14:54.930 --> 00:14:59.520
It Special Summons a Valkyrie from my hand.

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:03.880
Valkyrie Erste, attack!

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.120
Jonouchi!

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:07.050
Jonouchi!

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.120
It's truly over this time.

00:15:11.420 --> 00:15:13.120
I don't think so!

00:15:13.120 --> 00:15:16.270
I activate my trap, Silver Dollar!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:22.760
It erases the damage to a monster with 1000 or lower attack points!

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:26.740
How’s that!  I won’t lose that easily!

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.110
But hope never lasts for long.

00:15:31.110 --> 00:15:35.180
Fine.  I'll set one card and end my turn.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.120
My turn!  I draw!

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.580
One of them is a monster card.

00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:46.720
But I activate Dangerous Machine Type-6's effect!

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:52.500
It’s another 3!

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:53.660
I draw one card!

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:57.950
All right!  I haven’t run out of luck yet!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:01.600
I activate the spell card, Roll of Fate from my hand!

00:16:02.430 --> 00:16:08.550
I draw cards equal to the number I roll, and remove the same amount from my deck!

00:16:09.830 --> 00:16:11.210
All right!  It’s a 6!

00:16:13.240 --> 00:16:14.160
I'll use this!

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.490
The spell card, Giant Trunade!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:20.250
All spell and trap cards return to our hands!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:26.330
I activate the trap, Apple of Enlightenment!

00:16:26.330 --> 00:16:27.820
What?

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.230
Traps should have returned to the hand!

00:16:30.230 --> 00:16:34.240
Apple of Enlightenment activates when it's removed from the field.

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:37.500
It lets me draw a card from my deck.

00:16:37.500 --> 00:16:42.890
When Loge's Flame leaves the field, its effect also activates.

00:16:43.240 --> 00:16:46.810
Come with the flames, Valkyrie Brunhilde!

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:54.790
Brunhilde gains 300 attack points for every Warrior and Dragon-Type monster.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.660
I don't think so!

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:02.960
I tribute Swordsman of Landstar to summon Maximum Six in attack position!

00:17:04.100 --> 00:17:09.100
And when it's Tribute Summoned, I roll a die!

00:17:09.610 --> 00:17:12.980
It gains attack points equal to the number I roll times 200!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:15.470
I rolled a 6, so it gains 1200!

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:20.830
I activate the spell card, Star Blaster from my hand!

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.460
I tribute a monster and roll a die.

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:30.130
I Special Summon a monster whose Level equals what I roll plus the tributed's monster's Level!

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:39.570
Sasuke Samurai is Level 2, and I rolled a 5.

00:17:39.570 --> 00:17:41.440
So I can summon a Level 7 monster!

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.010
Come, Red-Eyes B. Dragon!

00:17:48.040 --> 00:17:50.340
Wow, Jonouchi!

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.490
He's attacking using dice!

00:17:52.490 --> 00:17:55.790
Maximum Six attacks Brunhilde!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:02.800
What?  Why wasn’t it destroyed?

00:18:02.800 --> 00:18:05.790
It’s Brunhilde’s effect.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:10.660
When it's attacked, it can lower its defense points by 1000 to avoid destruction.

00:18:11.910 --> 00:18:12.840
Red-Eyes!

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:26.960
I set the Dangerous Machine Type-6 that returned to my hand.

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:31.980
I set one card and end my turn.

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:35.930
How’s that!  Your fate is like a candle in the wind!

00:18:35.930 --> 00:18:37.620
Nice, Jonouchi!

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:38.640
He did it!

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:45.110
No one's ever made me this serious.

00:18:45.110 --> 00:18:47.500
I'll show you no mercy!

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.040
It's my turn!  I draw!

00:18:49.900 --> 00:18:53.280
I activate the Equip Spell, Enchanted Sword Nothung!

00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:58.370
I equip it on Brunhilde to raise its attack points by 400!

00:18:58.910 --> 00:19:01.920
Nothung is no ordinary sword.

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:03.850
This sword slays dragons.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:04.970
What?

00:19:04.970 --> 00:19:05.790
That's right.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:13.000
All Dragon-Type monsters on your field are destroyed and removed from play.

00:19:13.000 --> 00:19:14.560
Red-Eyes!

00:19:15.680 --> 00:19:19.620
I activate the spell card, Rainbow Bridge Bifrost!

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:27.810
For each of your monsters that was removed from play, my Valkyrie gains 500 attack points!

00:19:27.810 --> 00:19:29.550
I see!

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:37.690
His strategy was to remove Jonouchi’s monsters from play to increase his Valkyrie’s attack points.

00:19:46.760 --> 00:19:48.440
I don't think so!

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:51.300
I flip over my set card, Compensation Mediation!

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:54.470
You still defy your fate?

00:19:54.470 --> 00:20:02.080
Be quiet!  You shuffle this card with two of your cards, and then I choose a card.

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:06.750
If I pick this card, the battle ends!

00:20:08.170 --> 00:20:10.520
I won’t lose this final test!

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:12.460
Then choose.

00:20:12.900 --> 00:20:15.450
Your fate is on the line.

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:18.900
Jonouchi...

00:20:19.450 --> 00:20:21.380
I choose...

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:23.740
That one!

00:20:32.990 --> 00:20:35.160
Your luck ran out.

00:20:35.820 --> 00:20:37.620
Go, Brunhilde!

00:20:37.620 --> 00:20:39.880
Along with the warriors' souls!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.760
No way!

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:51.420
Jonouchi lost.

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:57.800
I told you.  Fate loves me.

00:21:01.970 --> 00:21:04.510
The winner is Sieg Lloyd!

00:21:04.510 --> 00:21:07.610
The Top 4 is now set!

00:21:07.610 --> 00:21:10.310
Too bad for Jonouchi.

00:21:12.740 --> 00:21:14.050
Jonouchi...

00:21:14.050 --> 00:21:17.830
Why did you choose the wrong card at the very end?

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:20.050
That’s not like you, Jonouchi.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:25.220
Maybe because he didn't have to risk his life in this duel.

00:21:25.220 --> 00:21:28.590
I see!  He only powers up when he's in danger!

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:30.750
Enough of that!

00:21:30.750 --> 00:21:34.060
Show me some sympathy!

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.180
C'mon!  Stop running!

00:21:37.180 --> 00:21:39.230
You almost won, Jonouchi.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.820
It was a good duel.

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:44.310
Yeah.  His opponent was powerful.

00:22:01.210 --> 00:22:15.830
Right now, we don't need a map

00:22:15.990 --> 00:22:31.550
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:37.390
Without a goal in mind

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:45.960
We just step towards our dream

00:22:46.350 --> 00:22:51.600
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:51.790 --> 00:23:00.070
Your eye will find it

00:23:00.430 --> 00:23:05.880
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:23:06.670 --> 00:23:14.020
Will touch your soul

00:23:14.210 --> 00:23:17.280
In a duel

00:23:29.480 --> 00:23:31.720
Jonouchi lost.

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:36.450
I guess he can't do his best unless something's on the line.

00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:40.460
Stop moping and let's go cheer for Rebecca!

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:43.280
It's Rebecca's semifinal match.

00:23:43.280 --> 00:23:46.440
What?  Yugi's grandpa is missing?

00:23:46.440 --> 00:23:51.580
He pulled his back, so he shouldn't be able to walk.  Where did he go?

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:54.080
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Rebecca vs Leon
Genius vs Genius

00:23:54.080 --> 00:23:55.730
Duel, standby!
